YouCoded License
================

YouCoded is licensed under the MIT License, the full text of which follows
below. This covers everything in this repository — the desktop application
(`desktop/`), the shared React user interface (`desktop/src/renderer/`), the
Android application (`app/`), build scripts (`scripts/`), and documentation
(`docs/`) — with one exception:

  • `terminal-emulator-vendored/` is a vendored copy of the Termux project's
    terminal-emulator library (github.com/termux/termux-app, itself derived
    from jackpal/Android-Terminal-Emulator). It is upstream code, licensed
    under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its license text and preserved
    copyright notices live at `terminal-emulator-vendored/LICENSE` and
    `terminal-emulator-vendored/NOTICE`; the Apache License requires that
    NOTICE to accompany redistributions of the library. See
    `terminal-emulator-vendored/VENDORED.md` for what was vendored and how.

Copies of the MIT text also live at `desktop/LICENSE` and `app/LICENSE`.

